{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_actor_and_cluster_panels", "label": "Actor and cluster panels", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_overview_panel", "label": "DevTools overview panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_actors_panel", "label": "DevTools actors panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_cluster_panel", "label": "DevTools cluster panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_cumulative_counters", "label": "Cumulative counters on the wire", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counters are cumulative on the wire and the UI derives per-second rates itself, so a browser that reconnects, throttles in a background tab or misses a tick still shows correct figures rather than a phantom spike."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_stopped_actor_tombstone", "label": "Stopped-actor tombstone", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stopped actor stays greyed out with a stopped-Ns-ago badge for 30 seconds because the actor you want to look at is usually the one that just died; removing its row the instant it stopped meant you never saw it. Remote trees get the same thirty seconds when an actor stops appearing in a round."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_hide_devtools_actors", "label": "Hide DevTools actors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DevTools runs its own hub and taps as ordinary actors, so they are real and therefore listed - but marked at spawn with ActorOptions.withInternal() rather than matched by name, so their children (a websocket connection is a child of its hub) are hidden too."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_ring_topology", "label": "Ring topology layout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every node gossips with every other, so the membership graph is complete and a force-directed simulation would only produce a slowly settling circle; a ring draws the same membership the same way every time."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_busiest_mailboxes", "label": "Busiest mailboxes list", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The fastest way from something is backing up to this actor is backing up."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_per_node_section", "label": "Per-node figure breakdown", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In a cluster every node runs a DevTools agent answering with its own numbers and the totals are their sum; a node that stops answering keeps its last reading marked not answering rather than disappearing, and is forgotten an hour later."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_charts_timespan", "label": "Charts over a chosen timespan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The series is recorded on the server from the moment DevTools attaches, so a panel opened an hour in shows that hour and a page reload does not lose it. Longer spans are bucketed; levels keep each interval peak so a spike survives summarising, and cumulative counters keep the interval last reading so the per-second maths stays correct however coarse the buckets are."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_split_y_axes", "label": "A level and a rate never share a y-axis", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On one scale a backlog of 400 flattens a 2-per-second line to nothing, so the three plots are split."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_removed_member_retention", "label": "Removed members kept for an hour", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The node that drops out of membership is the one you want to look at, and it used to disappear at exactly that moment; the record lives on the server, so reloading the page - often the first thing you do - does not erase it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_live_state_dot", "label": "Live actor state dot", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lifecycle events only announce births, deaths and restarts and nothing announces a suspension, so the tap re-inspects the tree each second and sends the cells that moved. A restart flashes the row because the path survives a restart and nothing else would move."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_actor_and_cluster_panels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_overview_panel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_actor_and_cluster_panels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_actor_visualizer_actors_panel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/actor-visualizer.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_con